#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167895} :activity/id #uuid "9f3fa68b-4b95-5afb-803a-30726de37cbc" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049381 :topic/id #uuid "f0242aed-46fd-5f2e-bcc2-49ee070cdccf" :topic/math-academy-id 3190} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167891 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167993 :tutorial/content "![](images/0b/0bebe0003d3d70b77be931f2dba651d85352bddf6e41b94055bb227b07d60153.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+5\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the result\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively.\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2s+5}{s(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) - 3 = - 2 \\left(\\dfrac{-2s+5}{s(s-1)}\\right) + 4 X_2(s) - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{3s^2-s-8}{s(s-1)(s-4)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{-2s+5}{s(s-1)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{5}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-5{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3{s}^{2}-s-8}{s(s-1)(s-4)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{3}{s-4}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\}-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}+3{e}^{4t}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{t}-5 \\\\ 2{e}^{t}+3{e}^{4t}-2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "00904ad0-6191-560b-a452-c838aa7543a6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14420 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "822d22ea-2253-5461-b518-1ae1ae238fee" :step/math-academy-id 590705 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167892}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167892 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166933 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166530 :question/id #uuid "008364d3-24bd-58e2-a8ab-f0d4d881e918" :question/math-academy-id "e-21575"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049877} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050801}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167222} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305121} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305124} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305125} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391080} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434056} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434057} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434059} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434060}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"} :step/id #uuid "3d8f9646-10b3-5bfd-97ef-e080e3440cfc" :step/math-academy-id 590706 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167893}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167893 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166531 :question/id #uuid "230e2550-b584-53fd-9da4-4128584124dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-21576"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167188} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167232} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305119} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308369} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308370} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308371} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434054} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434063} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515576} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515593}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"} :step/id #uuid "6351ca80-d1fa-5039-94d0-87986551c3b2" :step/math-academy-id 590709 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167894}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167894 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166532 :question/id #uuid "748ef205-542b-5763-9cdd-00dc9ff1d181" :question/math-academy-id "e-21577"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050768}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167189} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167233} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308390} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308391} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385173} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434058} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434061} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434062} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506573} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506578} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515563}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"} :step/id #uuid "5d6348a1-6da4-5516-b665-5319df7cd619" :step/math-academy-id 590712} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167895 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168032 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve inhomogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/e0/e04825ebe3b670d020df9c4dad9b86564a57542effc88b77d5778f535e15d5bf.svg)\n\nSimilar to the homogeneous case, the process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find initial variables \n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." :tutorial/id #uuid "3733acd7-1a13-5183-a501-0baf1eaf53a5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14611 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "91a3017f-8462-5088-8b1f-303f10ce818d" :step/math-academy-id 590715 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167891}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166988}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506621} :activity/id #uuid "acf80487-30da-5578-b5d8-3413af242da3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049381 :topic/id #uuid "f0242aed-46fd-5f2e-bcc2-49ee070cdccf" :topic/math-academy-id 3190} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506606 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4faa0bc1-0f83-5df5-b327-6631924a3461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3t}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506046}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506046} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a780d4-7f5e-5121-9749-f435d4e070d4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506399} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82f32ceb-ba57-523c-9952-b5724c0a4bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^{2t}-2e^{3t}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506138} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d556ca-1ce9-5f66-b4a1-85148a156058" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a2d20627-2f13-5baa-ae6b-0096d23c5fcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-333135" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)-8 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+9,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2{e}^{3\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =-2{e}^{3t}+3{e}^{2t}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{3t}+3{e}^{2t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1354470f-5d1a-53f8-82af-628f52a8a45f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506621 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "446d2e37-da3b-5ec4-9e85-ed0778e2a047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506026}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506026} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea6e246f-4955-529f-bde2-787eeb20b921" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "25f77b6f-c4e6-577f-be11-94654e67ed25" :question/math-academy-id "q-330955" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2 & ={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s}-2 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3-2s}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =1-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =1-(\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-1)-3+2s}{s(s-1)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s-3+2s}{s(s-1)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "43aab161-e695-57a7-8969-5ee8f4c6d017" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506652}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506630 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3e6253-cb2f-51e3-a09f-722442297438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506269}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506269} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ca1bb4c-a167-5a9d-a3af-6cd2b38386a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a5fa96f-7d32-5292-9419-4df3266355da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-e^{2t}+1+3e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506034} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ba858c4-352a-5ccd-b2f2-ddf2cb9c2ccb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "afb0fc7e-4ba2-590c-909f-dbefd260c961" :question/math-academy-id "q-333125" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2\\cdot t}+1+3{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{4t}-{e}^{2t}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ 3{e}^{4t}-{e}^{2t}+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "69795229-d4bd-5f42-bbf9-ca3a1404c6ec" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506606}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506652 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac964228-37ed-5165-995d-548c80a4f24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303520} {:answer/id #uuid "c12e4719-ad23-58b9-a060-4357d834aedf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}e^t-1+\\frac{3}{2}e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506260}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506260} :answer-field/id #uuid "20b81a8b-8f51-59ce-bf0d-1a13def57610" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304154} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf736de-0666-5d9b-968f-218e1f2297c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{t}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303701} {:answer/id #uuid "e83c20e7-16a6-544d-a4ca-f01a743529f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^t-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506336} :answer-field/id #uuid "f768c9da-81c3-54d5-8f63-a3d84cc7ca94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05245fe3-011d-5dbc-b60f-1afb740f2732" :question/math-academy-id "q-330958" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d17d556a-f8ce-5c71-aba6-473c775f92dd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506656}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506656 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0039aee6-98b7-59c0-8d03-5b2d50aa3e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305152}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305152} :answer-field/id #uuid "0377913c-e842-526c-a0d1-86f1c0379261" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3c4c091-3098-5cdd-a98e-d6a345ec5978" :question/math-academy-id "q-333070" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{2}(t)+2\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+2L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3(\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-5)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d632b05d-a89a-5460-91b8-ea467b225b71" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506630}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505910}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515683} :activity/id #uuid "f434441f-b9c7-5ee6-aaa1-b1b2afd5d471" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049381 :topic/id #uuid "f0242aed-46fd-5f2e-bcc2-49ee070cdccf" :topic/math-academy-id 3190} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515627 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515056} :answer-field/id #uuid "029ce416-5248-5a5e-a914-f27e3f878e0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333060" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}$ ,$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{4{x}_{1}(t)-3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =2-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-(\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)})-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-(2s-3)-s(s-4)}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s+3-{s}^{2}+4s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0d621a8f-cd0d-51e8-81b6-9ebdb390477f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515697}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515656 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "836205cc-5a3f-59ff-b85b-57b4914eb6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306406}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306406} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a865178-7308-51f1-b0b9-0385a7f16eef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "330e1019-3a7b-578b-a870-9a3ed163159a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1+{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305632}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305632} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7279e72-7b0d-5ec9-8874-4267900baa48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94146fce-5a5d-5f8d-9ed4-34e48238a883" :question/math-academy-id "q-333138" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =-1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -1+{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "590ff66c-34e8-5381-aeda-9ccba67a75bc"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515683 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e75c2a5-efac-57be-8e90-38a4d983daed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515132} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc222a5-fba5-54b1-8499-8bdfb1e8616c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "95759fde-a83b-52c8-a112-ac2f3137ea76" :question/math-academy-id "q-332776" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-4\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-4L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3 & =2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & ={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & ={X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-1)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-2)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-4}{s(s-1)(s-2)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b1745bc0-7e7d-5cce-a4e0-1fadf2d21096" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515627}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515690 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43cd4f5c-08fd-5bbb-8ca5-7564ab540dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305818}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305818} :answer-field/id #uuid "a11cf526-3ad2-5d27-b464-c2dc1021fed5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb7af99f-f087-5140-92ed-ce44ed5c2329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306897} :answer-field/id #uuid "d625bed8-e9e7-5e12-a73f-2e476aeb6a2e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "12cb134e-509f-512f-9761-fbb450604687" :question/math-academy-id "q-333133" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}+3{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}+3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c1ab16a5-ba62-5d1f-b985-9e65b24b08aa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515656}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515697 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d22d6e-0616-586f-b9f3-42b8d530fd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515140}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515140} :answer-field/id #uuid "0560274e-eedd-5cd3-a9f0-b7e672a7b4b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f2f8e1b-7ba5-5978-8caf-e60c554b76cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2e^{2t}+e^{3t}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515209}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515209} :answer-field/id #uuid "49de807c-da2e-59f0-b447-3aed1873fc9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "78ae591d-ba8b-5d77-97cc-75f76d82b6a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-333128" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2\\cdot t}+{e}^{3\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-2{e}^{2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-2{e}^{2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cd1c018d-a850-5621-b116-c5c0cc1a8c99" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515690}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514867}]}
